Marvel's MCU has had an incredible run  starting off in 2008 with the Seminole  Ironman the franchise has grown to  become the biggest cinematic universe in  movie history  the creative team have pushed the  boundaries in several ways and whilst  their work is often imitated it is  unrivaled after watching through the  entirety of the MCU twice yes  twice I've ranked the film's from worst  to best this was a labor of love and  took a lot of time so whether you agree  or disagree with my list please let me  know your favorites without the way I'm  definition and this is my ranking of the  MCU door the weakest of the MCU Thor  centers around the origin of the god of  thunder starring Chris Hemsworth Natalie  Portman and Anthony Hopkins this film  tells the tale of Thor traveling to  earth after being cast out of his realm  as God suffering from an underdeveloped  love story and wick third act  Thor fails to really deliver on the  quality that the MCU has been known for  The Incredible Hulk The Incredible Hulk  was a course correction from the  previous Angley version starring Ed  Norton and distributed by Universal this  movie feels almost alien to the rest of  the MCU and once the film start off  excellently it devolved into a rather  banal and predictable climax that makes  it easily skippable in the overall run  Ironman to the weakest of the Ironman  trilogy this film suffered heavily due  to the writers strike I still really  enjoy it but this clearly problems in  the film and this is definitely the  worst Black Widow performance this movie  struggles with a sophomore curse and  feels like a step down from the seminal  film that preceded it Thor the dark  world Thor the dark world has gotten  better with age but it's still  criminally under uses it's film and  feels like a stopgap between Avengers  movies it betters these of its  protagonists as opposed to its  predecessor but certainly doesn't do  enough good to rank higher in this list  shame as there's a lot of cool character  moments that really make the god of them  they're infinitely more endearing  Captain America the First Avenger the  only period piece from the MCU Captain  America the First Avenger perfectly  introduces one of Comics longest-running  characters featuring a brilliant villain  in Red Skull his film depicts the cat  taking on Nazis in World War two it  completely deconstruct how cap was used  as propaganda in the war whilst nailing  down the fundamentals of what it takes  to be a hero this lays the groundwork  for what is to come and there's a  brilliant job with the source material  Iron Man 3  Iron Man 3 deals with a lot of heavy  subject matter such as post-traumatic  stress disorder and politics were it not  for the neck jerking twist that comes at  the film's midpoint this movie would  rank a lot higher it features astounding  action scenes and balances the drama  beautifully with comedy it's just a  shame that there was some inexcusable  choices that means this movie ranks far  down the list Doctor Strange Doctor  Strange introduces magic to the MCU and  does so in stunning fashion the  incredible visuals and performance by  Benedict Cumberbatch really captured my  imagination on first viewing and this  film has stayed with me over time  relying rather heavily on the Marvel  formula and being quite derivative of  Batman Begins early on keeps this film  below the rest but there's still a lot  to like here  guardians of the galaxy vol 2 guardians  2 misses out on meaning more due to its  clear derivative aspects of The Empire  Strikes Back this is a fun film but it  fails to capitalize fully on its  predecessor emotionally feeling  shallower points I struggle slightly  with this film but there's a lot of fun  aspects that evolved the characters in  more ways than one and anything with  baby grouping deserves some credit and  Matt ant-man heavily follows the Marvel  formula  but poles are often a much better way  than dr. strange does in my opinion  laced with jokes this comedy is  laugh-out-loud funny and has the visual  flair to match never before had we seen  a character that was able to shrink down  to atom size and the unique perspective  that the hero provides makes this an  endearing film in what is cinemas  biggest franchise age of Ultron age of  Ultron is a guilty pleasure of mine it  develops a central cast in more ways  than one and features amazing battle  scenes such as the opener and Hulkbuster  fight this film really pits  Tony against the rest of the team and  starts the divide that would come to  fruition in Civil War disliked at the  time due to the amount of plot threads  that leaves dangling this film works  better in retrospect and definitely  deserves a revisit now that we have all  of the information on the table  guardians of the galaxy  guardians was a huge risk for Marvel  this cast of characters were practically  unknown to all but the most die-hard  Marvel fans due to amazing casting and  raised a job writing the Guardians were  able to stand center stage in the MCU  and compete with the a-listers that  surrounded them the film made several of  its stars household names and is  hilarious from start to finish  it also teases a lot of what is to come  and is as good today as it was upon  release Captain America the Winter  Soldier Captain America the Winter  Soldier is a conspiracy theorists dream  possessing huge reveals from start to  finish this film really cemented cap is  one of the most remarkable characters in  the MCU and it's a blast from beginning  to end  centering around the captain's  relationship with former ally Bucky  Barnes the movie has a heart to it that  is near unrivaled it would go on to play  a hard part of the Marvel Universe and  definitely feels more adult in tone than  the other films in the genre making it  better every time you watch it black  panther black panther now stands as one  of the highest-grossing movies ever made  it's no surprise as the story has a  superhero like no other and a complex  villain that provides a lot of  thought-provoking discussion on aspects  such as race and revolution I was blown  away by the film upon first viewing and  the  stands as a milestone not only for its  phenomenal profit but also for the fact  that it is the first film to really  bring representation of Africa to  Hollywood in such a positive light  spider-man homecoming spider-man  homecoming is by far the best webhead  movie ever made this highschool centric  film perfectly captures Peter Parker  having to deal with his dual identity  whilst trying to live a normal life  Michael Keaton delivers a standout  performance as the antagonist and  there's several action scenes that  beautifully showcase Spidey's full range  of abilities this one isn't to be missed  and this outstanding coming-of-age story  is relatable on many levels that cement  it as one of the best Thor Ragnarok Thor  Ragnarok completely reinvents the  Thunder God character and is all the  better for it  playful apps this futuristic AES retro  action-adventure takes a lot of the  right boxes and manages to incorporate  several legendary graphic novels such as  Planet Hulk beautifully into its arc  Jeff Goldblum will have you  side-splitting  cog will have you on the floor and by  the film's end you will view the  characters in a way like never before  this film works great on several levels  and is a blast from start to finish  Ironman the first film in the MCU really  knocked it out the park in my opinion  Ironman is a masterpiece in terms of  casting pace and effects it nails the  Marvel formula right off the bat and is  a character defining journey from  beginning to end well I love about  Ironman is that it captures your  imagination from the get-go and leaves  you wanting more the movie beautifully  teases the Avengers but to works  perfectly is a standalone piece I can't  really fault the film and this is one of  the best The Avengers  The Avengers film was a trendsetter  responsible for all shared universe  films that would try and copy it success  this still stands as the best the  dialogue provided by Joss Whedon is  perfect and it cannot be credited enough  for the influence that would have on  films and the comic book genre following  its release this was a worldwide  phenomenon and was a landmark moment in  movie history that has argued  one of its most important the film was a  bouncing act but it manages to pull it  all off perfectly and catapults this  film to the forefront Avengers infinity  war ten years in the making  Avengers infinity war is an ambitious  crossover that manages to succeed in its  goals of uniting the Marvel Universe to  tackle the threat of Thanos beautifully  paced acted and presented the film is an  instant classic due to the bills  relatability and the epic battle scenes  that span it's two and a half hour  runtime I was blown away by how poetic  and emotionally charged the film was and  somehow it balances all of this gravitas  with a humorous side that will appeal  even to the most stone-hard infinity war  is an incredible triumph and one of the  best Marvel films ever created Captain  America Civil War Captain America Civil  War is incredible from start to finish  picking the Marvel cast of characters  against one another it perfectly  balances action with drama and has many  thought-provoking aspects that discuss  how all actions have consequences  both sides of the argument have their  pros and cons and it's easy to get  caught up in debates of privacy and  foreign policy when watching this film  at its heart this is a story of  friendship and it's one that I  constantly come back to because of its  incredible character development  it introduces spider-man black panther  and much more and it's my favorite MCU  film  as with all of my lists I'd love to hear  your thoughts what's your top five have  you seen infinity war and if so what did  you think of the film as always you can  comment below and let me know make sure  you subscribe to my channel as I do  movie discussions and interpretations  weekly and they'll definitely be  something on the channel that you love I  recently created a Snyder cup version of  the Justice League using several of the  deleted scenes from the film so make  sure you check that out if you enjoy  comic book movies as always I'm  definition thanks for watching and I'll  see you next time take care peace  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

